<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:45:36Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="/atoms/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nepal: Thousands still missing as death toll rises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c992b4078b818231dd0532014f0ccdf608b111fc2f8871be0137ffb59214266</id><updated>2026-08-30T13:52:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T10:04:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-death-toll-rises--19b14e275677.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-death-toll-rises" /><summary type="html">Nepalese authorities announced on Sunday that the provisional death toll from the devastating floods had risen to more than 730, with nearly 2,500 people still missing.

Among the thousands of people missing is the husband of a 22-year-old woman, who is still waiting for him to return. Like tens of thousands of Nepalese people in recent days, she went to one of the country’s medical centres to find out whether her husband was among those whose bodies had been recovered in recent days. Caitlin Brown reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Glacial collapse leaves 3,000 missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b09a025583b7d3b5da31db5dd632af856ebf23b55ce9891d054bf165a7aa5670</id><updated>2026-08-30T13:52:52Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:16:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-glacial-collapse-leaves-3-000-missing--bf2b04c1f945.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-glacial-collapse-leaves-3-000-missing" /><summary type="html">Rescue and relief efforts in Nepal and Tibet have been hampered this Sunday by heavy rain and rising river levels. The latest figures following Wednesday’s flash floods put the death toll at 750, while more than 3,000 people remain missing. Nepal’s disaster authorities are urging rescue teams to “exercise caution”, warning that bad weather, swollen rivers and the threat of further flooding could hamper operations. Shazab Wahlah reports from the town of Bidur.</summary></entry><entry><title>Death toll rises as 3,000 remain missing in Nepal, China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc534c9e31271f2e8e55f343a9c8aa452751ee154ed6bdc6416c0b20d4b9ed9a</id><updated>2026-08-30T13:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T08:37:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/death-toll-rises-as-3-000-remain-missing-in-nepal-china--6a7e3695e252.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/death-toll-rises-as-3-000-remain-missing-in-nepal-china" /><summary type="html">Rescue and relief efforts in Nepal and Tibet have been hampered this Sunday by heavy rain and rising river levels. The latest figures following Wednesday’s flash floods put the death toll at 750, while more than 3,000 people remain missing. Nepal’s disaster authorities are urging rescue teams to “exercise caution”, warning that bad weather, swollen rivers and the threat of further flooding could hamper operations. Shazab Wahlah reports from the town of Bidur.</summary></entry><entry><title>Putin, Xi set for Central Asia summit as Russia and China seek to counter Western influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d70b2cc4e6b9c10c30a0eb7f94efaecb4463eae58cdd5575a78863baccbf400f</id><updated>2026-08-30T13:53:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T05:51:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-putin-xi-set-for-central-asia-summit-as-russia-china-seek-to-counter-western-influence--62e15ee5debd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-putin-xi-set-for-central-asia-summit-as-russia-china-seek-to-counter-western-influence" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin and Chinese President Xi Jinping are due in Kyrgyzstan on Monday for a two-day summit, joined by the leaders of Iran and India. The gathering comes as the group seeks to project a united front amid wars in Ukraine and Iran and growing tensions with the West.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal-Tibet floods live: Nepal begins mass burials as flood death toll surpasses 780</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e65c1a0e9457dba467316a05114784462e3c8a760c2db8acf491f2fad676d5b0</id><updated>2026-08-30T13:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T04:59:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-nepal-tibet-floods-live-at-least-750-dead-as-death-toll-rises--8e74f89e9cff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-nepal-tibet-floods-live-at-least-750-dead-as-death-toll-rises" /><summary type="html">Nepal on Sunday began temporarily burying some of the hundreds of bodies recovered from devastating floods after taking DNA samples and marking the remains so families can identify and retrieve them later. Rescue efforts entered a fifth day, with heavy overnight rain and rising rivers hampering attempts to reach hydropower workers believed to be trapped in tunnels. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Missing toll from Nepal, China flood nears 3,000 as race for survivors continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b01f596c8cfdfb9323577434e403bd8bc051b644e7489dcb7a40ca6bfc64a8a6</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:00:20Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T20:12:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260829-missing-toll-from-nepal-china-flood-nears-3-000-as-race-for-survivors-continues--011d0bbdf6ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260829-missing-toll-from-nepal-china-flood-nears-3-000-as-race-for-survivors-continues" /><summary type="html">Rescuers in Nepal and China on Saturday continued to search for the nearly 3,000 people missing after devastating flooding along the border with China engulfed entire villages earlier this week. At least 682 bodies were recovered in both countries, including 675 in Nepal and seven in China.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>‘Extremely risky operations’: Rescuers work amid threat of river banks bursting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6410e510402d44552c274860c1e3ca506ca5f0cef00f92dac21b21e40f9af06d</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:00:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T15:22:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/extremely-risky-operations-rescuers-work-amid-threat-of-river-banks-bursting--71fe5095c630.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/extremely-risky-operations-rescuers-work-amid-threat-of-river-banks-bursting" /><summary type="html">Nearly 3,000 people remained missing on Saturday, while 682 deaths had been confirmed after flash floods and landslides hit the Nepal-Tibet border. Rescue operations remain risky as a lake formed upstream by the floods threatens to burst its banks. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rescue operations ongoing as death toll continues to rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:665b4a928dc23997f217438ae6db199a7de46602a022af8a8da0d0835bec46c6</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:00:26Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T12:37:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/rescue-operations-ongoing-as-death-toll-continues-to-rise--58c55377d6ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rescue-operations-ongoing-as-death-toll-continues-to-rise" /><summary type="html">Most arrive with nothing except the clothes they are wearing. As rescue efforts in communities buried by catastrophic flash floods along the border between Nepal and China entered their fourth day Saturday, authorities continued finding survivors and transporting them to safety. At relief centers, as some arrive, families wait anxiously for news of their loved ones as the death toll and the number of people unaccounted for continued to rise.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepali army uses helicopters to rescue flood survivors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f10819f80514847599e31708cbc9e9878df6beb01825d20e2ae0a729ff6834d6</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:00:29Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T10:32:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/nepali-army-uses-helicopters-to-rescue-flood-survivors--db6798aa1af5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepali-army-uses-helicopters-to-rescue-flood-survivors" /><summary type="html">With roads damaged by the deadly floods, the Nepali army is using helicopters to carry out rescue operations and transport survivors to safety. Meanwhile, skies remain overcast, with more rain expected in the coming hours, raising concerns about further flooding. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal army races to rescue more than 100 trapped in hydropower tunnel after floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c8195d26823b88c0e10c32664e67eb1737e49d5803aa1bceb865f9581b69757</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:00:32Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T08:50:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-army-races-to-rescue-more-than-100-trapped-in-hydropower-tunnel-after-floods--2034486870f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-army-races-to-rescue-more-than-100-trapped-in-hydropower-tunnel-after-floods" /><summary type="html">Nepali army rescue teams were using drilling equipment on Saturday seeking to rescue more than 100 people trapped inside a hydropower tunnel, three days after devastating floods struck the site.</summary></entry><entry><title>UN, Nepal warn of climate threat after flood death toll tops 680</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:476f9599b7bfa4cc771c6f197109a3994c3ec4b811e042c2e2fd4979338d70ac</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:00:35Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T05:06:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260829-nepal-tibet-floods-live-death-toll-passes-600-nearly-2-500-people-still-missing--1f3e59acefbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260829-nepal-tibet-floods-live-death-toll-passes-600-nearly-2-500-people-still-missing" /><summary type="html">Nepal's foreign minister and the UN climate chief on Saturday warned of the growing threat from climate change to the Himalayas, three days after devastating floods swept along the border with China, engulfing entire villages. At least 675 people were killed in Nepal, according to the country's disaster authority. Another seven people were confirmed dead in Tibet, Chinese state media reported. Read our blog to see how all the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Families cling to hope as nearly 1,000 remain missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36fd687e779bd721ba86bfd563b4c2f7faf6ac393578b74d153ee8aac5a93907</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:45:33Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T16:56:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-families-cling-to-hope-as-nearly-1-000-remain-missing--d90124379841.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-families-cling-to-hope-as-nearly-1-000-remain-missing" /><summary type="html">Nepal's confirmed death toll has risen to at least 538, but families are still searching hospitals and disaster zones in the hope their loved ones will be found alive, with nearly 1,000 people still missing. More than 3,700 people have been rescued so far, though destroyed roads, bridges and thick mud continue to hamper search efforts.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Relief camp shelters grieving families</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54b0e88f8da2f0d9486ed10d25f9cb3de349273cedd64a91adb40dd94804ce6e</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:45:36Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T16:20:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-relief-camp-shelters-grieving-families--251bec211f6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-relief-camp-shelters-grieving-families" /><summary type="html">Around 500 people are sheltering at a monastery-turned-relief camp in northern Kathmandu, where many families are still in shock after losing their homes and loved ones in the devastating Nepal floods. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah reports from the camp as rescue teams continue searching for nearly 1,000 missing people, with operations set to continue through the night.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rescuers grapple with a mountain of challenges after the Nepal-Tibet floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9cd7047fa17c4b873c13bd2a4ab720bfa037ee39f11b9cd2b61e0e134eada28</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:00:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T14:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-rescuers-grapple-with-mountain-of-challenges-after-the-nepal-tibet-floods--bbaa37403151.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-rescuers-grapple-with-mountain-of-challenges-after-the-nepal-tibet-floods" /><summary type="html">Emergency services are rushing to find survivors and treat the wounded after a devastating flash flood on the border of Nepal and Tibet on Wednesday killed more than 500 people, with over a thousand still missing. But the remote and rugged terrain, as well as the risk of further flooding from upstream lakes formed by piles of debris, make their work as delicate as it is dangerous.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal floods explained: The chain of events behind the disaster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1dce178b4b3b35029f633a6b96de4bb58f5aaeda72c5da880be27b0b8bc6e9a7</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:00:47Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T12:48:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-floods-explained-the-chain-of-events-behind-the-disaster--5ab0173979c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-floods-explained-the-chain-of-events-behind-the-disaster" /><summary type="html">A glacier broke apart. An ice and rock avalanche followed. Then came an earthquake, before a landslide triggered devastating floods that tore through kilometres of valley. This is what happened along the Nepal-China border, where rescue teams are still trying to recover survivors 48 hours after the catastrophe. FRANCE 24 breaks down the chain of events and the scientific explanations behind the disaster.</summary></entry><entry><title>Japan's controversial WWII heroes: How one kamikaze pilot escaped certain death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:340f0c3c821b9e0e03ca7462b4148846aa443ad146f947e9865469577948ba0c</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T12:42:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260828-japan-s-controversial-wwii-heroes-how-one-kamikaze-pilot-escaped-certain-death--ad0c943dfef7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260828-japan-s-controversial-wwii-heroes-how-one-kamikaze-pilot-escaped-certain-death" /><summary type="html">Towards the end of World War II, as US troops advanced across the Pacific, Japan resorted to a desperate strategy: kamikaze attacks. Thousands of Japanese pilots, with an average age of just 21, were ordered to crash their explosive-laden planes into enemy ships. More than 3,800 pilots gave up their lives, killing over 7,000 allied naval personnel. Our reporter Mélodie Sforza met one of the last surviving former kamikaze pilots.</summary><category term="Revisited" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal flood survivors rescued from hydropower tunnel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7457a91c6666d2c0b338a7e2ed72af30c24d62d098bb7dcf890f9e92dd6dfa1c</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:00:53Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T12:38:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-flood-survivors-rescued-from-hydropower-tunnel--4ef4567d0335.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-flood-survivors-rescued-from-hydropower-tunnel" /><summary type="html">Nepali soldiers rescued around 100 people trapped inside a flooded hydropower tunnel as the death toll from the Nepal-China floods continued to climb, with more than 1,500 people still missing. Rescue efforts were briefly suspended over fears that an overflowing landslide lake could trigger more flooding, while families across the disaster zone continue searching for loved ones.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Ran for our lives': Flood survivors recount terrifying escape from Nepal-Tibet disaster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:343951e9ff4af837f74aebb6b6cc225e81f938c991afb8f47db68bfe5962df03</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T11:55:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-ran-for-our-lives-flood-survivors-recount-terrifying-escape-from-nepal-tibet-disaster--9062a87ff517.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-ran-for-our-lives-flood-survivors-recount-terrifying-escape-from-nepal-tibet-disaster" /><summary type="html">Survivors of the catastrophic flash floods in Nepal and Tibet, some still missing friends and family members, shared harrowing accounts of their escape from raging floodwaters that brought devastation to the Himalayan border region, leaving more than 550 people dead and some 1,500 missing.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal and Tibet : around 93,000 people affected, according to the Red Cross</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcba52f9391832a782fd92f97c0b116e07c5791e3bcf2e16e1d00d604cb6a783</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:01:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T11:42:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-and-tibet-around-93-000-people-affected-according-to-the-red-cross--b7a85ae690ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-and-tibet-around-93-000-people-affected-according-to-the-red-cross" /><summary type="html">The death toll continues to rise in the Nepal and Tibet floods as the situation remains fast-moving. The Red Cross says around 93,000 people have been affected. International aid is arriving from several countries, but rescue efforts have been hampered by the difficulty of coordinating operations in the remote Himalayan terrain. The epicentre of the disaster was only reached 48 hours after the floods began. FRANCE 24's Jamie Smith-Maillet has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Army rescues hundreds trapped in tunnel as flood risk reignites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8dcfd9c26e8c02b7537417743b13836434ce7d87775a0ebda5c95c3a0041f11d</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:01:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T10:36:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260828-nepal-army-rescues-hundreds-trapped-in-tunnel-as-flood-risk-reignites--6a1581161ea0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260828-nepal-army-rescues-hundreds-trapped-in-tunnel-as-flood-risk-reignites" /><summary type="html">#Rescue operations are underway in #Nepal after devastating #floods killed hundreds and left more than 1,400 missing. The #RedCross has also raised concern over humanitarian #aid, as it estimates nearly 100,000 people were affected by the #disaster.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal flash floods: 'Very challenging' for survivors who have lost their homes and their families</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9639275bf7067526cb597bf5d5b274b96c715ef16372cd54b7aef7bb491668a1</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:01:05Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T09:50:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260828-nepal-flash-floods-very-challenging-for-survivors-who-have-lost-their-homes-and-their-famil--d407f7f07ee1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260828-nepal-flash-floods-very-challenging-for-survivors-who-have-lost-their-homes-and-their-families" /><summary type="html">Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Sunita Sharma, Head of Programs of Karuna-Shechen. While Nepal has considerable experience responding to natural disasters, the scale of the present devastation exposes a deeper challenge: Placing greater emphasis on preparedness. The immediate priorities are clear: finding those still missing and providing survivors with drinking water, food, shelter, clothing and medicine. But recovery cannot end there. Ultimately, they will need to rebuild confidence and entire communities. Given the scale of the destruction, that process could take years.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal flood disaster reconstructed minute by minute</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86c9ac765ff68ebe95471cfc9586861d560cdc9a161426146dc5e557e9bcf66f</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:01:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T09:22:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-flood-disaster-reconstructed-minute-by-minute--630d562069f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-flood-disaster-reconstructed-minute-by-minute" /><summary type="html">New satellite imagery and video analysis show the deadly Nepal floods began when part of a glacier near the Chinese border collapsed, triggering a debris flow that raced downstream at up to 150 km/h and devastated communities over more than 80 kilometres. Scientists are still piecing together the exact sequence of events, while authorities warn the disaster may not be over as a newly formed lake upstream has started to overflow.</summary></entry><entry><title>China's lost children: Adoptees search for answers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8524fe0dd03d3fbe96fd0770319fc7dadd5ea69ebbd980e5b36288bb7ade37b5</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:01:11Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T09:19:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260828-china-s-lost-children-adoptees-search-for-answers--11157e51a175.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260828-china-s-lost-children-adoptees-search-for-answers" /><summary type="html">At the height of China's controversial one-child policy, children were torn away from their birth families and put up for adoption. FRANCE 24's Yena Lee follows one adoptee, now an adult, who is on a quest to find out more about her background.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>In Tibet and Nepal, 'the most pressing fear is that the death toll could rise'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b61f2374e03f0aaed47208bdbb6039a7293f16e07b69117ff15489cda5c94981</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:01:15Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T09:16:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/in-tibet-and-nepal-the-most-pressing-fear-is-that-the-death-toll-could-rise--62847bb99648.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/in-tibet-and-nepal-the-most-pressing-fear-is-that-the-death-toll-could-rise" /><summary type="html">At least 472 people have been killed and more than 1,500 remain missing after devastating flash floods hit the Himalayan border between Nepal and China, where over 3,250 people have already been evacuated by helicopter. As rescuers race to find survivors, one of the biggest fears is that the death toll will continue to rise, with authorities also warning that an overflowing lake upstream could trigger more flooding. FRANCE 24's Navodita Kumari has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Countries step up aid for Nepal flood disaster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3dbbd945f63c130d463fcb1a2117e0cddcb17e0910e11f19921da1925a8acd51</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:01:17Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T09:00:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/countries-step-up-aid-for-nepal-flood-disaster--2a6b2e4020fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/countries-step-up-aid-for-nepal-flood-disaster" /><summary type="html">Countries including South Korea, India, China, the UK and the EU are ramping up rescue efforts and humanitarian aid after the devastating Nepal-China floods, with hundreds of foreign nationals still missing. Relief operations remain difficult in the Himalayan terrain, while authorities warn that a lake formed by the disaster could burst and trigger a second wave of flooding.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rescuers search for hundreds still missing in Nepal-Tibet disaster area as death toll climbs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d950851b348ae3f9bd17c622d4e179e273e9cda3b04e5540805cc4c4257e8f8</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:01:20Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T03:03:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-nepal-tibet-live-china-warns-lake-formed-by-mudslide-on-nepal-border-could-breach--bc3684962263.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-nepal-tibet-live-china-warns-lake-formed-by-mudslide-on-nepal-border-could-breach" /><summary type="html">Rescuers in Tibet reached the main area wiped out by a devastating mudslide this week, Chinese state media reported, as the search for missing people battled treacherous conditions. The devastating flooding in Nepal and Tibet has claimed more than 580 lives and left more than 2,400 missing. Read our live blog to see how all the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Number of people missing in deadly Nepal, Tibet floods jumps past 2,400</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ffb90090113378b6a52e75763327245db524aaf53f246a5b8b0a5b972e68d38</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:01:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T02:45:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-number-of-people-missing-in-deadly-nepal-tibet-floods-jumps-past-2-400--1ea066221dcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-number-of-people-missing-in-deadly-nepal-tibet-floods-jumps-past-2-400" /><summary type="html">Nepal’s disaster authority sharply raised the number of missing to 1,924 on Friday, including 517 foreigners, two days after devastating floods that killed at least 586 in the country. A further 558 people are also reported missing in Tibet, where Chinese officials say at least five people have died.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Red Cross mobilises in Nepal following natural disaster: 'Entire villages &amp; communities washed out'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb01e59e83a9dc498debdb1dbf7fc92a129b2d3ddaddecccb531c3812062b304</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:01:26Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T17:53:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/red-cross-mobilises-in-nepal-following-natural-disaster-entire-villages-communities-washed-out--47aa95bed8e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/red-cross-mobilises-in-nepal-following-natural-disaster-entire-villages-communities-washed-out" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Tommaso Della Longa, Spokesperson for the International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies. The immediate challenge in Nepal is not only the scale of destruction, explains Della Longa, but the difficulty of reaching communities whose roads, bridges and communications have been swept away. Their priority remains search and rescue and the delivery of life-saving assistance, even as they begin preparing for longer-term recovery. Yet this is also a deeply human crisis for first responders: local Red Cross volunteers are supporting their own communities while some have themselves lost homes or relatives.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pakistan: Protests continue in Azad Kashmir despite repression and internet blackout</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84dd7dd4399c5610f6ebcd359a1dcc2aabbf7d1b23a1e7d631247f273d83c339</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:01:29Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T16:04:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260827-pakistan-protests-continue-in-azad-kashmir-despite-repression-and-internet-blackout--5c9cfbef56bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260827-pakistan-protests-continue-in-azad-kashmir-despite-repression-and-internet-blackout" /><summary type="html">Harshly repressed protests that have shaken Pakistan-administered Kashmir since early June have continued through local legislative elections held in July and August. With internet access cut off and access by foreign media restricted, local residents are attempting to report on the situation on the ground.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Why were so many Indian pilgrims in Tibet during the Himalayan mudslide disaster?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e846f483a519b7a60dfc03f48099deb1ed4075faf7782f0bc7471439c9773d1</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:01:32Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T13:57:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.france24.com/en/why-were-so-many-indian-pilgrims-in-tibet-during-the-himalayan-mudslide-disaster--4c87b0ccdc3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/why-were-so-many-indian-pilgrims-in-tibet-during-the-himalayan-mudslide-disaster" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of Indian nationals are missing in Nepal and Tibet following a catastrophic Himalayan flood. They include several pilgrims doing the Kailash Mansarovar Yatra pilgrimage to Mount Kailash, a mountain in Tibet that holds sacred significance for Hinduism, Buddhism, Jainism and the Tibetan Bon religion, explains FRANCE 24’s Leela Jacinto.</summary></entry></feed>
